  "notes": [
    "Exercises the core browser-control read, wait, locator, input, scrolling, snapshot, highlighting, and script/style methods against one deterministic localhost fixture.",
    "The fixture has no external resources, random values, timestamps, animations, or platform-specific text, and every mutating action has an independent DOM state probe.",
    "A bounded startup settle precedes browser creation because the control socket can become ready before the desktop owner window is registered; that readiness race is tracked separately from browser semantics.",
    "No platform differences are pre-approved; exact capture pointers may be classified only after frozen-canonical and Windows behavior have both been reviewed."
  ],
